values ('b9c0d1e2-4f5a-4b59-8c89-9d0e1f2a3b99', 'social-work-practice-with-individuals-and-families', 'Social Work Practice with Individuals and Families', 'Supervised generalist methods for working with individuals and families across engagement, assessment, planning, intervention, crisis response, referral, evaluation, and termination. Students practice relational and interviewing skills; CBT-informed, solution-focused, motivational, and family-systems strategies; trauma-informed and anti-oppressive care; ethical reasoning; documentation; technology use; case coordination; supervision; and feedback-informed improvement. Person-in-environment, strengths, human rights, safety, culture, and structural conditions organize the course.');

